# --- px63: the disk -----------------------------------------------------------
# The block device and the block layer reach the self-test and the file
# system's suite; the file system, the tree's second store and the mount
# reach mpx6-ext2 and every user suite (they run programs over the tree:
# @user). The disk's tools and its recordings are mpx6-ext2's by the
# derivation (the test names them); its probes reach mpx5-users too,
# which reads user/elf. (@disk is defined with the groups above.)
kernel/vblk/*                   @disk
kernel/block/*                  @disk
kernel/ext2/*                   mpx6-ext2 mpx6-part mpx6-root mpx6-journal mpx6-nodes @user
kernel/fstab/*                  mpx6-ext2 mpx6-part mpx6-root mpx6-journal mpx6-nodes @user
# px68: the journal is kernel/ext2's, and reaches what ext2 reaches.
kernel/journal/*                mpx6-ext2 mpx6-part mpx6-root mpx6-journal mpx6-nodes @user
tools/blk-pattern               mpx6-blk
tools/e2fs                      mpx6-ext2
tools/mkdisk                    mpx6-ext2
tools/e2tree                    mpx6-ext2
tools/linux-blk                 mpx6-ext2
tools/mkdiskprobe               mpx6-ext2
user/elf/disk.c                 mpx6-ext2
user/elf/reboot.S               mpx6-ext2
# px66: the partition table. kernel/block (@disk, above) reads it and
# serves /proc/partitions through kernel/procfs (@user, and mpx6-part's
# rows); the table's tools, the guest's questions and the disk that boots
# are mpx6-part's (by the derivation too: tests/mpx6-part names them);
# tools/mkdisk and its tools are mpx6-ext2's as well (it names them).
kernel/procfs/*                 mpx6-part mpx6-root mpx6-nodes
tools/mkgpt                     mpx6-part
tools/disktools                 mpx6-part
tools/linux-part                mpx6-part
user/disktools.pin              mpx6-part
user/fstab-disk                 mpx6-part
# px67: `/` on the disk. The suite's probe, its builder and the Linux
# guest's tool are mpx6-root's by the derivation (tests/mpx6-root names
# them); /proc/self/mounts and mountinfo are kernel/procfs' (above). The
# crash row was reported, never gated (px67); px68 gates it in
# tests/mpx6-journal's J7, whose script names it (and its tools,
# tools/mkjournal and tools/jorder, by the derivation).
tools/root-crash                mpx6-journal
# px79: the block devices' nodes. kernel/files serves them (open, raw
# I/O, the ioctls, mount(2) by node) and kernel/user sends a write to
# one, so both reach mpx6-nodes beside @user; kernel/procfs's /sys block
# files are its too (above). Its probe, the probe's builder and the
# Linux guest's tool are its by the derivation (tests/mpx6-nodes names
# them); it reads tests/mpx6-part's `full` fixture.
kernel/files/*                  mpx6-nodes
kernel/user/*                   mpx6-nodes
tests/mpx6-part.d/fixtures      mpx6-nodes
# px67: the root-on-disk legs. Ten suites' jobs boot their ISOs a second
# time with `/` on a disk (tools/rootdisk-leg, through
# tools/qemu-rootdisk, after the suite's own step): mpx3-boreutils,
# -console, -shell, -threads, -maps and mpx5-users whenever they
# run; mpx5-pelt, mpx4-lobo and mpx5-jobs, the contract's long ones, only
# outside `tier pr` (the job's own `if`). Both tools, and tools/mkdisk's own, reach those nine by the
# derivation (each job's block names tools/rootdisk-leg). The other
# suites have no such leg: mpx3-tree's stores are the memory tree's
# (its probes on a disk root measure ext2 against Linux's tmpfs: a
# directory's 4096 bytes and 8 blocks for tmpfs's 40 and 0, the limits,
# the census; CI run 40059322645), mpx3-user and mpx3-loader boot kernels with
# no tree on a disk to read, the screen and sound suites' rows are their
# devices', and the disk suites (mpx6-*) bring their own disks or are
# the root's own (mpx6-root).

